  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1142 PM CDT FRI AUG 7 2026\n\nThis evening, Central Alabama remains in a somewhat weak upper \nflow area south of the main broad trough that extends out of  \nCentral Canada and down into the Great Lakes. At the same time, \nAlabama is situated between two ridges, one across the Four \nCorners and the other in the Western Atlantic off of the FL Coast.\nThe difference from yesterday is that guidance is now showing a \nsmall developing shortwave moving in from the northwest. While\nthis will not make a huge difference, it should orient our highest\nrain chances to the northwest/north areas for Sat/Sun. Our\nemphasis will still be typical summertime diurnally enhanced \nconvection overall. By Monday, the Western Atlantic ridge \nflattens and retrogrades further westward across the Northern \nGulf Coast. At the same time, it also shows the upper shortwave \nabsorbed back into the longwave trough with just continued \nsummertime diurnally enhanced activity expected through the \nremainder of the week.\n\nAs for temperatures, readings vary only a degree or so here and \nthere over the next week with overall moisture remaining up. This \nwill result in max afternoon heat indices perhaps a couple of \ndegrees higher in spots. However, guidance continues to keep us \nbelow heat advisory criteria for now. \n\n08",
